    "summary": "Martial compresses the same episode into a four-line epigram: Arria hands Paetus the blade with 'non dolet' ('it does not hurt'), adding that what does hurt her is the wound he is about to make. A distinct, more condensed poetic treatment than Pliny's prose letter, from a different genre entirely.",
