    "textEdition": "Text: Karl Jacoby, ed., Leipzig: Teubner, 1885–1905 (as digitized by Perseus). Abridged: omits the digression on Brutus's name, ancestry, and feigned folly at 4.68–69, and the kinsmen's private deliberation in 4.71",
    "title": "The Death of Lucretia",
    "tradition": "Roman",
    "period": "Composed c. 7 BCE",
    "setting": "Late Roman monarchy under the Tarquin dynasty, traditionally dated c. 509 BCE",
    "deathMode": "Suicide",
